          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ജനൽ — janal — \"a window\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തീവണ്ടിയുടെ ജനലിലൂടെ ഞാൻ വയലുകൾ കണ്ടു. tīvaṇṭiyuṭe janalilūṭe ñān vayalukaḷ kaṇṭu. Through the train window I saw the paddy fields."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also spelt ജനാല. A window seat is a ജനലിനടുത്തുള്ള സീറ്റ്."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ജനൽ (janal) was borrowed from Portuguese janela, a window, one of the words the Portuguese left on the Malabar coast."
            }
          ]
        },
